From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ed Watson <ew@cellink.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3399-rock-4c-plus: add OP-TEE firmware node

Add the firmware/optee DT node so that the kernel OP-TEE driver
(drivers/tee/optee) probes correctly and creates /dev/tee0 and
/dev/teepriv0 devices.

The kernel 6.6 rk3399.dtsi has a root-level psci node but no firmware {}
wrapper and no optee child node. Without this node the OP-TEE driver has
no DT match and does not bind, even though BL31 + OP-TEE (BL32) are
already loaded and running in TrustZone secure world from the SPL FIT image.

Verified against linux-6.6.y: rk3399.dtsi line 200 has a bare psci node,
neither rk3399.dtsi nor rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts contains a firmware node.

Upstream-Status: Submitted
Signed-off-by: Ed Watson <ew@cellink.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-rock-4c-plus.dts
@@ -703,3 +703,12 @@ &vopl_mmu {
 &vopl_mmu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/* OP-TEE Trusted OS firmware node.
+ * Required for the kernel TEE driver (drivers/tee/optee) to probe and
+ * create /dev/tee0 + /dev/teepriv0. OP-TEE is loaded as BL32 by SPL.
+ */
+/ {
+	firmware {
+		optee: optee {
+			compatible = "linaro,optee-tz";
+			method = "smc";
+		};
+	};
+};
